WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.493
Today is six round letters. None of them starts with a line.

2
00:00:03.943 --> 00:00:10.755
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:11.255 --> 00:00:12.360
These six letters.

4
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.539
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

5
00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:21.209
Here is the first one. Start high, on the right. Curve back, and around. Then stop.

6
00:00:22.465 --> 00:00:26.815
All the others begin with that same curve. That is why they are one family.

7
00:00:27.415 --> 00:00:30.692
This one: curve around, close it, go up, and come down.

8
00:00:32.276 --> 00:00:36.330
This one: curve around, go up tall to the top line, and come down.

9
00:00:37.709 --> 00:00:42.157
This one has a tail. Curve around, go up, come down below the line, and hook.

10
00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.131
This one: curve around, and close it at the top.

11
00:00:47.727 --> 00:00:51.688
And this one: curve around, go up, come down below the line, and flick.

12
00:00:52.188 --> 00:00:56.746
In words, this letter always has the same partner. Together they sound like this.

13
00:00:58.164 --> 00:01:05.280
A round letter that starts with the curve comes out facing the right way. A round letter that starts with the line often flips.

14
00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.892
Your child finger-traces all six, saying each path.

15
00:01:09.342 --> 00:01:16.689
Then press play on the listening track for job two, and step away. Your child reads four words, and the voice says each one.

16
00:01:19.818 --> 00:01:20.853
The word is cat.

17
00:01:21.753 --> 00:01:26.312
In job three, your child traces the letters and writes those same four words.

18
00:01:26.762 --> 00:01:30.611
At the end, they write two letters and one word while you watch the pencil.
